Subject: [PROPOSED P19 SR6] mfreadwrite: complete asynchronous pre-start Flush

Microsoft documents OnFlush on async completion, without a pre-start
exception. The injected P18 control returns S_OK but never calls OnFlush.
Use the existing serialized flush operation even while the source is stopped.

The queued-seek early return remains a separately unqualified interaction;
this patch does not claim all concurrent Flush/seek combinations are repaired.
Not in a candidate series; runtime and cross-route qualification pending.

--- a/dlls/mfreadwrite/reader.c
+++ b/dlls/mfreadwrite/reader.c
@@ -3574,7 +3574,7 @@
     unsigned int stream_index;
     HRESULT hr;
 
-    if ((reader->flags & SOURCE_READER_ASYNC_SEEK_QUEUED) || reader->source_state != SOURCE_STATE_STARTED)
+    if (reader->flags & SOURCE_READER_ASYNC_SEEK_QUEUED)
         return S_OK;
 
     if (reader->flags & SOURCE_READER_FLUSHING)
